flowchart TB

INGROW["`INGESTION — the top of the diagram`"]

UP["`UPLOAD — four validations before
anything is persisted:
extension against an allowlist
declared MIME type · byte count
magic bytes
an executable never enters the system
files are never executed`"]

STORE["`MINIO
object under a UUID key:
subject id + extension
original filename ignored
cheaper than S3: no per-request,
no egress · swap = endpoint + credential`"]

INGEST["`CELERY INGEST WORKER — in order:
fetch from MinIO → convert to Markdown
→ header-aware chunks of ~1,000 chars
with overlap → embed each chunk
→ index in PostgreSQL
only then status = indexed`"]

SAFE["`BUILT TO SURVIVE CRASHES
idempotent task · acks-late →
at-least-once delivery
progressive retries 15, 30, 60 s
still failing → status failed +
Dead Letter Queue in Redis
no infinite retries, no stuck queues`"]

VDB["`PostgreSQL + pgvector
1,024-dim embeddings stored natively
HNSW index · cosine distance
what Pinecone or Qdrant would do,
without one more system to operate`"]

GWROW["`AI GATEWAY — the center`"]

GW["`THE SINGLE DOOR
no module calls a provider SDK directly —
imposed by the architecture: providers live
behind an interface in infrastructure
centralizes: fallback · circuit breaker
· concurrency limit · cost ledger`"]

TSTD["`STANDARD TIER — the call that DECIDES
roadmap, roadmap repair, the judge
Claude claude-haiku-4-5
→ OpenAI gpt-oss-120b
→ Ollama llama3.2:3b`"]

TFAST["`FAST TIER — bulk work over a
decision already made (the tokens live here)
Nova nova-lite
→ OpenAI gpt-oss-20b
→ Ollama llama3.2:3b
Claude is OUT of this chain on purpose`"]

BED["`AMAZON BEDROCK
three model FAMILIES, one vendor,
one credential — a bad key removes
the remote half of the chain
model variety kept, vendor variety dropped`"]

CB["`CIRCUIT BREAKER — per family
closed → 3 failures → open
→ 30 s → half-open
state lives in REDIS, not in memory:
the whole fleet shares 'this provider is out'
invariants: Ollama can never be disabled
· at least one remote family stays active
LLM calls never hold a DB connection`"]

GENROW["`PLAN GENERATION`"]

GEN["`ownership check → AI budget check
(once per plan) → planner drafts the
roadmap (sync, standard tier)
⇄ roadmap reviewer criticizes — judge by AI
code-level checks first, LLM judge only
on a weak signal · roadmap materialized
only when valid — no orphan rows`"]

FAN["`FAN-OUT — one task per academic item
30+ units of work, fast tier
each retrieves its own context
per unit: all fails or nothing fails
invalid roadmap → nothing persisted
item fails later → partial continue`"]

PDF["`OUTPUT
source endpoint shows exactly the passages
the model received: ranking · document
· title · section header
Markdown → HTML → WeasyPrint PDF
LaTeX for tables and charts`"]

RETROW["`RETRIEVAL — the bottom of the diagram`"]

EMB["`query embedded with the SAME model
that embedded the document — bge-m3,
multilingual, 1,024 dims, same vector
space, same cosine distance
~24x slower, chosen for recall quality`"]

HYB["`HYBRID SEARCH — two in parallel
vector search: understands MEANING
lexical search: Postgres text index —
exact terms: acronyms, codes, law numbers
('Lei 9394' vs 'Lei 9610')`"]

RRF["`RECIPROCAL RANK FUSION
combines by POSITION, not score —
cosine and lexical live on different
scales, positions are comparable
validated on real questions:
hybrid had the best recall
retrieved content = DATA, not instruction`"]

INGROW -.- UP
UP --> STORE --> INGEST --> VDB
INGEST -.- SAFE
GWROW -.- GW
GW --> TSTD
GW --> TFAST
TSTD --> BED
TFAST --> BED
GW -.- CB
INGEST -->|"embeddings"| GW
GENROW -.- GEN
GEN --> FAN --> PDF
GEN -->|"standard tier"| GW
FAN -->|"fast tier"| GW
RETROW -.- EMB
INGEST -.-|"same model, same vector space"| EMB
EMB --> HYB --> RRF
FAN -->|"retrieves context"| HYB
VDB --> HYB

